a. provide services;
b. provide protection to victims of acts of violence, reporters and witnesses; and
c. conduct empowerment of victims of acts of violence.
(2) Services as referred to in paragraph (1) letter a include:
a. receive complaints/reports of violence against women and/or children, consultation, and counseling;
b. receive and send case referrals from District/City Regional Governments or institutions established by other District/City Regional Governments;
c. provide legal assistance and accompaniment;
d. health;
e. social rehabilitation;
f. legal aid services; and
g. repatriation and social reintegration.

